[size=4][b]Wrath Build Planner[/b][/size]

Follow a character build from a guide without comparing every level by hand. Import the build as a small text file, assign it to a character, and press [b]Apply build[/b] in the level-up or character-creation window. The mod makes that level's picks in the game's own window; you look them over and press Complete yourself.

[size=3][b]Create a build with ChatGPT or Claude[/b][/size]

You do not need to write the file yourself. The build page turns any guide into a build with the chat AI you already use:

[url=https://gh05d.github.io/wrath-build-planner/]https://gh05d.github.io/wrath-build-planner/[/url]

[list=1]
[*]Copy the prompt from the page and paste it into ChatGPT, Claude or any other chat AI, together with the guide's text or table.
[*]Paste the AI's answer back into the page. It checks every class, archetype, feat and spell name against the game and tells you what to fix — with a ready-made message for the AI.
[*]Copy the result and use [b]Paste from clipboard[/b] in the mod's Builds window.
[/list]

The Builds window links to the page, too.

[size=3][b]How it works in the game[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Open the Builds window with the new HUD button or Ctrl+P (the key can be changed in the mod settings).
[*]Import a build: [b]Paste from clipboard[/b], or put a [i].json[/i] file into [i]Mods/WrathBuildPlanner/Builds/[/i].
[*]Assign it to your main character or a companion. During character creation (main character or mercenary), click the build name or [b]Set build…[/b] in the bar at the bottom of the window.
[*]On every level-up press [b]Apply build[/b]. A list shows what was set and, for anything that could not be set, why — with similar names when a name was not found.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The mod never finishes a level for you, and it only fills what is still open — picks you made yourself stay.
[*]Class, race, starting ability scores and alignment are always set from the build. Portrait, appearance, voice and name are always yours.
[*]After applying, the window steps forward to the first page that still needs you.
[*]Names can be written in English even when the game runs in another language.
[*]Content added by other mods works: the mod matches names against what the game offers on the page at hand.
[*]Mythic ranks and mythic paths are supported; a path is only chosen when the game offers it.
[*]Using AutoLevelUp as well? Give a companion a build in one of the two mods, not in both.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Mouse and keyboard interface only (no gamepad UI).
[*]Builds are not edited inside the game — change the file and press [b]Reload folder[/b].
[*]Companions keep the levels they join with; a build applies from their next level.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Installation[/b][/size]

Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/21]Unity Mod Manager[/url]. Install the zip with UMM (or extract it into the game's [i]Mods[/i] folder). An example build is included in [i]Builds-examples[/i].

Source code: [url=https://github.com/Gh05d/wrath-build-planner]github.com/Gh05d/wrath-build-planner[/url]
